//****************************************************************************
// $Module type: Dialog
// $Module name: DemoData
// $Author     : Nils Svedmyr, RDC Tools International, <mailto:support@rdctools.com>
// Web-site    : http://www.rdctools.com
// Created     : 2026-10-10
//
// Description : The data-aware classes on DataFlex's own two code tables: a cFTDbModalPanel with two
//               cFTDbCJGrid grids on the left - the code types, and the chosen type's codes - and a
//               cFTDbGridHost on the right, whose web fields are bound to the chosen type and whose
//               cFTWebList shows the same codes. Each side alone is a dialog of its own: DemoDataCodeJock.dg
//               and DemoDataWeb.dg.
//
// This code is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY;
// without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.
//****************************************************************************
Use Windows.pkg
Use cFTDbModalPanel.pkg
Use cFTDbCJGrid.pkg                 // RDCToolsLib's data-aware grid in the FT look
Use cRDCDbCJGridColumn.pkg          // its column
Use cFTLocalWebControlHost.pkg      // a web control needs a host Used before it
Use cFTGridHost.pkg                 // the button bar's host
Use cFTDbGridHost.pkg               // the data-aware host, on the same grid of 8 px columns
Use FTAllWebControlClasses.pkg      // cFTWebForm, cFTWebList, cFTWebButton - and the framework's cWebEdit
Use FTPageIsUp.pkg                  // FTHostPageIsUp - can the host's page take a live push now?
Use cCodeTypeDataDictionary.dd      // CodeType - it makes sure the two tables are there
Use cCodeMastDataDictionary.dd      // CodeMast, a type's codes

/* TWO DATA DICTIONARIES, NATIVE CONTROLS ON THE LEFT AND WEB CONTROLS ON THE RIGHT (the data-aware classes at
   work). CodeType and CodeMast are the two code tables DataFlex gives every workspace: a type with a
   description and a comment, and the codes of a type. The demo copies the empty tables into its Data folder
   the first time it runs and adds a few rows (DemoCodeTables.pkg).

   The left column is native - CodeJock grids:
   - oTypes_grd, a cFTDbCJGrid on the CodeType DD: the types. A row chosen there is the DD's record. A
     description is changed in place, and the down arrow on the last row adds a type.
   - oCodes_grd, a cFTDbCJGrid on the CodeMast DD, which the CodeType DD constrains: the chosen type's codes.
     Type in a cell to change one; the down arrow on the last row adds one; Delete removes one; the row is
     saved when it is left.

   The right column is ONE web host, oTypeHost, a cFTDbGridHost:
   - web fields bound to the CodeType DD with Entry_Item, as a dbForm is - so they show the chosen type and
     follow the grid. The comment is text of several lines, in the framework's own cWebEdit: the library has
     no class for it, and it takes the FT look from the host. Save is the framework's own Request_Save, which
     the host carries out on its Server, the CodeType DD: a FlexTron data-aware host is a data-entry client,
     as a Windows view is, so it moves what was typed in the bound fields into the DD and has the DD validate
     and save it. Clear is its Request_Clear.
   - Clear, beside Save, adds a NEW type from the web side (Nils 2026-10-10), as the grid's own new row does
     from the native side: the DD lets go of its record, the fields empty, the grid on the left gets an empty
     row - the CodeJock grid does that itself when its DD is cleared by another control - and the Type field,
     shut for a type that exists, can be typed in. Save then saves the new type, and the grid's row takes it.
     That the key is typed for a new type only is the DD's rule (DD_COMMIT), so the grid's Type column and
     the web field agree.
   - oCodes_lst, a data-aware cFTWebList on the CodeMast DD: the same codes as the grid beside it, as a web
     list. Its columns are bound with Entry_Item, and it fills itself from the DD - no OnManualLoadData. It
     shares the DD with the grid, so the two follow each other: a row chosen in one is the DD's record, and
     the other shows it; a code added or changed in the grid is in the list once it is saved.

   The DDs belong to the panel, a cFTDbModalPanel, so the grids and the host share them. Each side alone is a
   dialog of its own: DemoDataCodeJock.dg (the grids) and DemoDataWeb.dg (the web controls). */
Object oDemoData is a cFTDbModalPanel
    Set Label to "Data-aware, mixed: code types and their codes"
    Set Location to 10 10
    Set Size to 282 430
    Set piMinSize to 282 430

    Object oCodeType_DD is a cCodeTypeDataDictionary
    End_Object

    Object oCodeMast_DD is a cCodeMastDataDictionary
        Set DDO_Server to oCodeType_DD
        Set Constrain_File to CodeType.File_Number
    End_Object

    Set Main_DD to oCodeType_DD
    Set Server to oCodeType_DD

    // ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the left column: native
    Object oTypes_tb is a TextBox
        Set Location to 6 10
        Set Size to 9 196
        Set Label to "Code types - a cFTDbCJGrid you can type in."
    End_Object

    /* The types: a row chosen here is the DD's record, and the rest of the dialog follows it.

       A NEW TYPE CAN BE ADDED HERE (Nils 2026-10-10): the down arrow on the last row appends an empty row - the
       grid clears its DD for it - and the row is saved when it is left. pbAllowEdit and pbAllowAppendRow say
       so; the library's class has both off. A description can be changed in place; the Type column takes
       typing in a new row only, because the DD says its key is committed once saved (DD_COMMIT,
       cCodeTypeDataDictionary.dd), and the grid asks the DD before it lets a cell be edited. Rows are not
       deleted here: a type has codes under it.

       NO CHECK BOX COLUMN, and that is the class's own default: phoCheckbox_Col and phoData_Col are -1, which
       its footer routine reads as "none". Leave them alone - 0 is not "none" there, and the routine then asks
       object 0 for a column (error 98 as the dialog opens, Nils 2026-10-10). The footer is this grid's own:
       how many types there are. */
    Object oTypes_grd is a cFTDbCJGrid
        Set Server to oCodeType_DD
        Set Location to 18 10
        Set Size to 110 196
        Set peAnchors to anTopLeftRight
        Set pbAllowEdit to True
        Set pbAllowAppendRow to True
        Set pbAllowInsertRow to False
        Set pbAllowDeleteRow to False
        Set pbAutoAppend to False
        Set Status_Help to "Choose a type. The down arrow on the last row adds one; a new type's name is typed in its first cell."

        Object oCodeType_Type is a cRDCDbCJGridColumn
            Entry_Item CodeType.Type
            Set piWidth to 110
            Set psCaption to "Type"
        End_Object

        Object oCodeType_Description is a cRDCDbCJGridColumn
            Entry_Item CodeType.Description
            Set piWidth to 220
            Set psCaption to "Description"
        End_Object

        // The class sends this whenever the row or the data changes; it writes the footer.
        Procedure DoSetCheckboxFooterText
            Integer iTypes
            Get_Attribute DF_FILE_RECORDS_USED of CodeType.File_Number to iTypes
            Set psFooterText of (oCodeType_Type(Self)) to ("Types:" * String(iTypes))
        End_Procedure
    End_Object

    Object oCodes_tb is a TextBox
        Set Location to 134 10
        Set Size to 9 196
        Set Label to "The type's codes - a cFTDbCJGrid you can type in."
    End_Object

    // No check box column here either (the class's default), and no footer: the grid has nothing to count.
    Object oCodes_grd is a cFTDbCJGrid
        Set Server to oCodeMast_DD
        Set Location to 146 10
        Set Size to 100 196
        Set peAnchors to anAll
        Set pbAllowEdit to True
        Set pbAllowAppendRow to True
        Set pbAutoAppend to True
        Set pbAllowDeleteRow to True
        Set pbShowFooter to False
        Set Status_Help to "Type in a cell. The down arrow on the last row adds a code, Delete removes one."

        Object oCodeMast_Code is a cRDCDbCJGridColumn
            Entry_Item CodeMast.Code
            Set piWidth to 110
            Set psCaption to "Code"
        End_Object

        Object oCodeMast_Description is a cRDCDbCJGridColumn
            Entry_Item CodeMast.Description
            Set piWidth to 220
            Set psCaption to "Description"
        End_Object
    End_Object

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- the right column: web
    Object oType_tb is a TextBox
        Set Location to 6 212
        Set Size to 9 208
        Set peAnchors to anTopRight
        Set Label to "The same data as web controls - a cFTDbGridHost"
    End_Object

    /* THE DATA-AWARE HOST: 8 px columns, as a cFTGridHost has. Column 16 takes the extra width, so the fields
       fill the host; Clear and Save, 11 columns each, end at its right edge. Row 8, the list, takes the extra
       height, so it grows with the dialog. The host's own Server is the CodeType DD - the fields' - and the
       list names the CodeMast DD as its own: a host holds controls of more than one DD, as a view does.

       AIR UNDER THE COMMENT (Nils 2026-10-10: the buttons sat too close to it). The Comment field spans rows 2
       to 4, and row 4 is 25 px where a row is 33, so the field is 8 px shorter; row 5 is those 8 px, empty.
       Clear and Save, in row 6, are where they were. */
    Object oTypeHost is a cFTDbGridHost
        Set Location to 18 212
        Set Size to 228 208
        Set peAnchors to anTopBottomRight
        Set piColumnCount to 39
        Set psColumnWidths to "16/1fr"
        Set psRowHeights to "4/25px 5/8px 8/1fr"
        Set Server to oCodeType_DD
        Set Auto_Clear_DEO_State to False   // the saved type stays chosen
        Set Verify_Save_Msg to 0            // no Windows boxes
        Set Verify_Data_Loss_Msg to 0

        /* THE TYPE'S KEY: shown for a type that exists - it is chosen in the grid, and a key is not changed -
           and typed in for a new one, after Clear. The field opens and shuts itself: a DD tells its controls
           whenever its record changes - a row chosen in the grid, Clear, Save - and this one asks the panel
           then (SyncTypeField). It starts shut: the dialog opens on the first type. */
        Object oType_wf is a cFTWebForm
            Entry_Item CodeType.Type
            Set Server to oCodeType_DD
            Set piRowIndex to 0
            Set piColumnIndex to 0
            Set piColumnSpan to 39
            Set piLabelOffset to 80
            Set psLabel to "Type:"
            Set pbEnabled to False

            Procedure Refresh Integer eMode
                Forward Send Refresh eMode
                Send SyncTypeField
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        Object oDescription_wf is a cFTWebForm
            Entry_Item CodeType.Description
            Set Server to oCodeType_DD
            Set piRowIndex to 1
            Set piColumnIndex to 0
            Set piColumnSpan to 39
            Set piLabelOffset to 80
            Set psLabel to "Description:"
        End_Object

        // Text of several lines: the framework's own cWebEdit, bound like the fields above. No cFT class - the
        // host gives it the FT look, its label's right justification too: it names no peLabelAlign.
        Object oComment_we is a cWebEdit
            Entry_Item CodeType.Comment
            Set Server to oCodeType_DD
            Set piRowIndex to 2
            Set piRowSpan to 3
            Set piColumnIndex to 0
            Set piColumnSpan to 39
            Set piLabelOffset to 80
            Set psLabel to "Comment:"
            Set pbFillHeight to True
        End_Object

        // Clear, to the left of Save: the fields emptied for a new type.
        Object oClearBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piRowIndex to 6
            Set piColumnIndex to 17
            Set piColumnSpan to 11
            Set psCaption to "Clear"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-eraser"
            Set psToolTip to "Empty the fields for a new code type"

            // After the web click has returned.
            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send DoClearType of (oDemoData(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        Object oSaveBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piRowIndex to 6
            Set piColumnIndex to 28
            Set piColumnSpan to 11
            Set psCaption to "Save"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-check"
            Set psToolTip to "Save the type - a new one, after Clear, or the description and the comment of the chosen one"

            // After the web click has returned.
            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send DoSaveType of (oDemoData(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object

        Object oCodesLabel is a cFTWebLabel
            Set piRowIndex to 7
            Set piColumnIndex to 0
            Set piColumnSpan to 39
            Set psCaption to "The type's codes - a data-aware cFTWebList"
            Set psCSSClass to "FtCompact ftaccent"
        End_Object

        /* THE DATA-AWARE LIST (Nils 2026-10-10: a data-aware cFTWebList beside the CodeJock grids). The main
           window's glyph list gets its rows from code; this one is bound: its Server is the CodeMast DD and
           its columns name their fields with Entry_Item, so the framework reads the rows from the DD - the
           chosen type's codes, since the CodeType DD constrains it - and reads them again when the type
           changes. pbDataAware is True by default; there is no OnManualLoadData here. A list shows; it does
           not edit - the grid on the left does that, on the same DD. */
        Object oCodes_lst is a cFTWebList
            Set Server to oCodeMast_DD
            Set piRowIndex to 8
            Set piColumnIndex to 0
            Set piColumnSpan to 39
            Set pbFillHeight to True
            Set piOrdering to 1                 // index 1: the type, then the code
            Set psPlaceHolder to "No codes yet"

            Object oCode_col is a cWebColumn
                Entry_Item CodeMast.Code
                Set psCaption to "Code"
                Set piWidth to 90               // 90 px
                Set pbFixedWidth to True
            End_Object

            Object oCodeDescription_col is a cWebColumn
                Entry_Item CodeMast.Description
                Set psCaption to "Description"
                Set piWidth to 1                // the rest of the list's width
            End_Object
        End_Object
    End_Object

    /* THE BUTTON BAR: a plain grid host - it holds no bound field - with Close at the right edge.

       ITS HEIGHT: one row of buttons is 33 px, and the Web UI theme pads a host's content by 4 px above and
       below - 41 px in all. A host shorter than its content scrolls, so at 20 units, about 33 px, this bar had
       a scroll bar (Nils 2026-10-10). 26 units hold the row at 100 % and above. */
    Object oButtonBar is a cFTGridHost
        Set Location to 250 320
        Set Size to 26 100
        Set peAnchors to anBottomRight
        Set piColumnCount to 12         // column 0, then Close's 11
        Set psColumnWidths to "0/1fr"

        Object oCloseBtn is a cFTWebButton
            Set piColumnIndex to 1
            Set piColumnSpan to 11
            Set psCaption to "Close"
            Set psCSSClass to "ftbtn ftg-close"
            Set psToolTip to "Close this dialog"

            Procedure OnButtonClick
                Send Close_Panel of (oDemoData(Self))
            End_Procedure
        End_Object
    End_Object

    /* The Type field is typed in for a NEW type only. The value is stored for a page that loads (Set) and
       pushed to a page that is up (WebSet) - FTHostPageIsUp: the host active, and its page has called home. A
       WebSet before then has nowhere to go, and the dialog finds its first type before that. */
    Procedure SyncTypeField
        Boolean bHasRecord

        Get HasRecord of oCodeType_DD to bHasRecord
        Set pbEnabled of oType_wf to (not(bHasRecord))
        If (FTHostPageIsUp(oTypeHost(Self))) ;
            WebSet pbEnabled of oType_wf to (not(bHasRecord))
    End_Procedure

    /* Clear and Save, from the web buttons (Save from Ctrl+S too): the type host carries out the framework's own
       request on its Server, the CodeType DD. Clear lets go of the record, and its controls follow - the fields
       empty, the Type field opens (its Refresh), the grid on the left gets an empty row, the codes go. A save
       leaves the DD with no changes to save - a save the DD refused leaves them, and its error has said why. */
    Procedure DoClearType
        Send Request_Clear of oTypeHost
        Send Focus of oType_wf
        Set StatusText to "A new type: enter it, and press Save."        // the panel's own status bar
    End_Procedure

    Procedure DoSaveType
        Boolean bChanged
        Send Request_Save of oTypeHost
        Get Should_Save of oCodeType_DD to bChanged
        If (not(bChanged)) ;
            Set StatusText to "The type is saved. A new type's codes go in the grid below the types."
    End_Procedure

    // The first type, when none is chosen yet - so the fields and the codes have something to show.
    Procedure Activating
        Boolean bHasRecord
        Forward Send Activating
        Get HasRecord of oCodeType_DD to bHasRecord
        If (not(bHasRecord)) ;
            Send Find of oCodeType_DD FIRST_RECORD 1
    End_Procedure

    // The panel's own Clear would empty the fields of a type that is still chosen in the grid.
    Procedure Request_Clear
    End_Procedure

    On_Key Key_Ctrl+Key_S Send DoSaveType
    On_Key Key_Alt+Key_C  Send Close_Panel
    On_Key kCancel        Send Close_Panel
End_Object
